From 74702035f354b91a10a317672bb608806a2a84c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:47:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nim/ac: CheckSysupdateAvailableSOAP, GetInitializeResult,
 SetFromApplication

Calls seen when StreetPass Mii Plaza goes online, previously answered by
the generic "unimplemented" fallback:

- nim:s 0x000A CheckSysupdateAvailableSOAP: now replies success with the
  "update available" flag set to 0. The fallback left that word as whatever
  was in the buffer, so apps could see an update (the Nintendo Zone viewer,
  for one, stops using the connection when an update is reported).
- nim:s 0x003F GetInitializeResult: success (NIM is ready).
- ac:u/ac:i 0x002C SetFromApplication: takes the value and ACConfig and
  hands the config back, like SetRequestEulaVersion.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
